    {
     "key": "main#389/6155958479:r3-disposition-repairs",
     "kind": "review-verdict-with-new-math",
     "statement": "The author's disposition of the five SIDE24 V3 main-text findings adds new mathematics in three places. (a) A repair argument for Lemma 3.4: self-attachment is restated as same-maximum, meaning both ascending half-branches of S end at M. If a half-branch instead ends at a different maximum in the same component of {f>h}, that maximum and M have a merge saddle with value in (h,b), so the case lies in B_r. The three regions are measured from the midpoint x, and the envelope (3.16) is stated to need the value-window constraint. (b) Re-scoping: (3.17) is stated uniformly on compact positive marks ",
     "status_in_post": "Planned r3 changes only. Nothing is pushed and the head stays at ff73d996. Status is HOLD_CAPACITY until the coordinator allocates the work. The author says r3 needs a substantive nonauthor read of the changed passages. Scientific effect NONE, credit 0. The repair argument is short (one step)."
    }
   ]
